You may install and use Yosr Dross for free, for personal and commercial work.

You may not copy, modify, redistribute, sublicense, sell, or reverse engineer Yosr Dross (the `dross` binary and the private source it is built from), except as the law allows. Installing it through the official Homebrew tap or the official release archives, and the copies your computer makes to install and run it, are allowed.

Your files stay yours. Yosr Dross claims no rights in your files, projects or caches.

Data. Yosr Dross does not collect telemetry or usage data, and it does not phone home to Yosr AI or check for updates. When you ask it to clean a named cache, it runs that tool's own command (for example `npm cache clean --force` or `dotnet nuget locals global-packages --clear`). That tool is not part of Yosr Dross and behaves under its own terms.

Third-party components. The `dross` binary includes open-source libraries under their own licenses (mostly MIT and Apache-2.0). Their notices are published in `THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md` at https://dross.yosr.ai/trust/ and in the release archive of each version that includes it. Nothing in this license limits your rights under those licenses.

Deleting files. Yosr Dross is a tool for removing files. By default it moves the folders you confirm to the macOS Trash, and it deletes permanently only when you choose that explicitly. You decide what is removed. Before you confirm a clean, check what it lists, and keep backups of anything you need.

